WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.034
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.135
to the Captain's quarters.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.370
As we told you yesterday,

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.906
Giant Lobster Nemesis
won our Twitter poll

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.908
for which Sea Captain B-plot
we should further explore

00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:11.143
and I want to assure you,

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.578
we're workin'
on writin' that up.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.548
Now, there was a fourth option
on the poll, called Other,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.851
and some of you have asked
what would've happened,

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:19.886
had that won.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.388
Well, I'll show you right now

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.624
because you guys really
dodged a bullet.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.393 line:0%
We were gonna
introduce a duck.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:30.096 line:0%
He was gonna be kinda like
a nebbishy,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.965 line:0%
neurotic Brooklyn-type duck,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.634 line:0%
who lives in the
Prospect Park duck pond

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.303 line:0%
and is always trying to talk
to you about his problems.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.238
-Being a duck is hard.
It's just like, you know,

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.173
people are always throwing
breadcrumbs at me

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.741
and it's like, you know,
I'm actually trying

00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:44.944
to lose weight, okay?

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:45.978
Quack.

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:47.914
-So just be grateful
Giant Lobster won

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.116
because, while many of you
hate the Sea Captain,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.952
all of you would've
despised the duck.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.587
-How do ya like me now?!

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.488
-And, hey, speaking
of the opposite of winning...

00:00:56.488 --> 00:00:58.324
-Reverse segue!

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.026
-...as our urgent
national health crisis

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.894
continues to deepen
with no end in sight,

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.397
the president has been calling
into friendly TV shows

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.033
to promise it will
magically go away

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.168
and Senate Republicans
have been holding hearings

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.938
on a made-up conspiracy theory
about the Russia investigation.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.307
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.977
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.546
Earlier this week, we found out
that our criminal president,

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:21.814
who, let's remember,

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.083
already benefited from two
criminal conspiracies

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.185
to interfere
in the 2016 election,

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:27.453
got impeached for trying

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.756
to orchestrate another one
in the 2020 election,

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.459
and is currently trying
to disrupt the election

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.561
by lying about mail-in ballots
and gutting the post office,

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:39.498
is also under investigation
for fraud.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.467
I know.
Try not to be too shocked.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.637
This guy collects fraud charges
like parking tickets.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.705
One day, he's gonna open up
the glove compartment

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.140
of his golf cart
and there's just gonna be

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.543
a bunch of warrants
for his arrest in there.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.111
Pretty sure half of the papers

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.580
he brought to his Axios
interview were summons.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.549 line:0%
[ As Trump ]
You know, if we're not
doing better

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.018 line:0%
than any other country
with testing,

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.587 line:0%
then why am I

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.756
"hereby summoned to appear"?

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:07.126
And, look, as not shocking
as a fraud investigation is,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.128
it's still a huge deal.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.496
And then, yesterday,
we found out

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:13.399
that Trump's bank was subpoenaed
by those same prosecutors,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.735
suggesting the investigation
of his business practices

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.505
is more wide-ranging
than we knew.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:21.774
Honestly, I'm just shocked his
business has any records at all.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.343
I bet if you open a file
cabinet at Trump Tower,

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.512
it's just a family
of hissing raccoons.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.081
[ As Trump ]
Do you want my tax returns
as much as you want rabies?

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.382
In any other world,

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.051
this would be the biggest
news story of the year,

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.620
but there's just barely
any room for it.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.889
Hey, remember how the news
used to end

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.492
with a cute story about a cat
who learned how to play piano

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.394
or some kid who found
a Mickey Mantle rookie card

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.661
in his grandma's attic?

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:44.363
Now, every newscast
basically ends --

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.300
We close tonight with a story
to make ya smile.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.336
The president has been selling
artifacts from the Smithsonian

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.704
to Kazakhstani warlords

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.739
and replacing them
with forgeries.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.840
Isn't that something, Deborah?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.375
[ Laughing ]
"It sure is, Ken."

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:57.643
We'll see ya tomorrow.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:03:00.546
Because even stories
of fraud and bank subpoenas

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:03.148
got swamped by the president
deciding to venture

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:05.551
out of his right-wing
media bubble earlier this week

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.453
to sit down
for the aforementioned

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.456
disastrous interview with Axios
that could've also doubled

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.825
as a intake exam
at a psych ward.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.026
Jonathan Swan,
the interviewer,

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.462
shoulda just held up
some inkblot tests.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.897
"And what do you see here?"

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.198
-It is what it is.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.200
-Okay.
That's very interesting.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.202
So, to regain some self-esteem,

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.972
Trump rushed back to the
friendly confines of Fox News,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.374
calling in for long,
rambling phone interviews

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.142
with Lou Dobbs
and the Fox &amp; Friends,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.411
where they'll let them get away

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.079
with any lie,
no matter how outrageous.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.082
And, when the topic of the
coronavirus pandemic came up --

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.684
you know, the deadly plague
that's currently killing

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:40.853
over 1,000 Americans per day --

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:44.123
Trump repeated one of his
most sociopathic lies.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.192
-My view is the schools
should open.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.094
This thing's going away.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:51.263
It will go away
like things go away

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.765
and my view is that schools
should be open.

00:03:53.765 --> 00:03:56.736
-Is he talking about a pandemic
or a summer romance?

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.571
[ As Trump ]
Oh, you know, we'll both
go back to school

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:01.073
and it'll go away,
like things go away.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.876
But then, I'll find out
you didn't go back to Australia,

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.744
but I'll play cool
in front of the T-Birds.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:07.246
You'll get mad.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.648
Anyway, open the schools.

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.484
And, seriously, just stop
saying stuff like that.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.685
You've been saying it
for six months

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.453
and it's been both wrong
and dangerous.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:15.787
Of course, you know,

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:18.056
if you're a New York City
real estate crook, like Trump,

00:04:18.056 --> 00:04:20.860
things really do just go away
because you probably have

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.162
a bunch of criminal goons
around you to make 'em go away.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.931
Trump probably just
never realized

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.065
that was what was happening.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.333
[ New York accent ]
Mr. Trump, you know

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.102
that pesky detective
who's been sniffin' around?

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.469
Let's just say he went away.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:31.971
[ As Trump ]
Oh, that's great.
He took a vacation?

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.939
[ New York accent ]
No, I mean he sleeps
with the fishes.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.008
[ As Trump ]
Oh! He has sex with fish?

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:39.979
-Hey, uh, Seth,
what has one thumb, a hook,

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.114
and has sex with fishes?

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.182
-I don't know.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.184
-This guy!
[ Laugh ]

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.552
-You're awful.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.987
-Well, at least I didn't just
kneel behind a painting

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:51.156
and take a picture
of my own thumb.

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:52.791
-Fourth wall, anyone?

00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:54.560
Seriously, you can tell
how much easier

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.062
the Fox interview was
than the Axios interview,

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:58.364
just from their faces.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.832
The Fox &amp; Friends look like

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.867
vacant spouses
in a loveless marriage

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.869
who stopped feeling
anything years ago.

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:05.003
I mean, look at 'em.

00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:06.339
They look like
they just caught a glimpse

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.739
of their reflection in a window,

00:05:07.739 --> 00:05:10.609
holding a bunch of shopping bags
from Saks Fifth Avenue,

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:13.345
and they're thinking,
"All the Fendi bags in Manhattan

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:14.980
won't fill the hole
inside of me."

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.582
Meanwhile, Swan looks like

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.384
his dog just got up
on his hind legs

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.785
and asked him for some money.

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.520
[ As Trump ]
I can't tell you
what it's for, Jonathan,

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.656
but I need it like yesterday!

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.024
At another point
in the Fox interview,

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.225
Trump claimed the country
was doing great,

00:05:27.225 --> 00:05:29.461
as long as you ignore
the parts that are really bad,

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.530
which is, you know,
most of the country.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.832
-You look at a map
and white means good.

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:38.204
Most of the -- most of the map
is in the white color.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:42.641
The red color is
the corona or potential

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:45.177
and it's a very relatively
small portion.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.212
-Yeah, just ignore
the red parts and we're fine.

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:50.216
Kinda how a plane crash is
actually a successful landing,

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.885
if you ignore everything
besides the black box.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:56.655
-Ah, what's the deal
with the black box?

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.292
They should make
the whole plane out of it!

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.927
[ "Seinfeld" theme sting plays ]

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.329
-As of today,
only eight more shows

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.629
with the Sea Captain,
I swear.

00:06:04.629 --> 00:06:06.231
-That's what you say!

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:10.069
You don't bring me with you,
there's gonna be a [bleep] riot.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.604
-Second, it's just not true

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.039
that the red parts
are a small part.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.474
Look at The New York Times
case map.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:17.643 line:0%
There are a ton of densely
populated areas in the Sunbelt,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.945 line:0%
you know, places where
lots of people live.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.647 line:0%
That's why the corona map

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.714 line:0%
looks like this map,

00:06:22.714 --> 00:06:23.949 line:0%
of where people live.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:26.319
We have a fourth
of the world's deaths

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:29.154
and we're still recording
50,000 cases a day,

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:31.423
while other major countries
are recording a few hundred.

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:33.459
You can't just take
a random part of the map

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.728
as a success story,
if no one lives there.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.763
[ As Trump ]
The Mojave Desert
has never been safer,

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.565
but the fake news
never mentions that.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.834
And yet, as shocking as this
blatant denial of reality is,

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:44.703
it's by no means unique
to Trump.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:47.072
It's endemic to the entirety
of the conservative movement

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:49.574
and the Republican Party,
and has been for a long time.

00:06:49.574 --> 00:06:52.211
For example, while Trump was,
once again, promising

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.546
that the pandemic
would magically disappear,

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:55.915
what were Senate
Republicans doing?

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.717
Were they rushing to extend

00:06:57.717 --> 00:06:59.952
the expired $600
unemployment benefit

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.420
or the eviction moratorium

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.423
or the Paycheck Protection
Program for small businesses?

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:05.724
Were they holding hearings

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:08.928
on the preventable deaths
of 160,000 Americans?

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.897
Nope!
They were pestering

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:13.398
former Deputy Attorney General
Sally Yates

00:07:13.398 --> 00:07:15.034
on their insane
conspiracy theory

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:18.303
that the Obama administration
spied on the Trump campaign

00:07:18.303 --> 00:07:20.606
to frame him in the
Russia investigation

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.576
and, not surprisingly, most
of their questions backfired.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:27.012
-You don't like Donald Trump,
do you?

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:29.715
-I don't like --
I don't respect the manner

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.817
in which he has carried out
the presidency,

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:35.287
-Okay. You despise
Donald Trump, don't you?

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.823
-No, I don't despise
anyone, Senator.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.691
-Miss Yates,

00:07:39.691 --> 00:07:44.497
when did you first become aware
that the Obama administration

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:49.568
was surveilling
the Donald Trump campaign?

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:51.036
-The Obama administration

00:07:51.036 --> 00:07:53.739
was not surveilling
the Donald Trump campaign.

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.611
-These guys are so easy
to checkmate.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.713
[ As Kennedy ]
You despise Donald Trump,
don't you?

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:02.915
What, you don't?
Well, well, now, what am I

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.417
supposed to do with the rest
of my five minutes?

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.051
That was my ace in the hole.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.354
And, Ted, you weren't prepared
with a follow-up?

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:09.555
You didn't think she'd just

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:12.058
shut down your [bleep] question
in one sentence?

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:13.826
"All right, Ted,
it's all on you today."

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.828
[ As Cruz ]
Don't worry, guys.
I got this.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:18.397
"I see you only have
one index card there, Ted."

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.032
[ As Cruz ]
Yep. That's all I need.

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:21.767
"You sure?"
[ As Cruz ] It's a lock.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:23.435
"What if it doesn't work?"
[ As Cruz ] Oh, it'll work,

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.403
or my name isn't Ted Cruz.

00:08:25.403 --> 00:08:26.472
"Isn't your name Rafael?"

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:27.506
[ As Cruz ]
Dammit!

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:29.474
Well, then, I'll just hide

00:08:29.474 --> 00:08:31.143
behind my facial hair.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:33.612
Trump is not unique
and he's not an anomaly.

00:08:33.612 --> 00:08:36.315
He's the culmination of decades
of conservative politics.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:40.085
His lawlessness, racism,
sociopathic incompetence

00:08:40.085 --> 00:08:42.288
are endemic to the entirety
of the modern Republican Party,

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.456
which is why it's
not enough to beat him.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.326
We have to fundamentally change
the system that produced him.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:48.460
We can't just pretend that,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.429
as long as Trump loses
in November,

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.231
the conditions that
created him will just...

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.700
-Go away, like things go away.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.302 line:0%
-Did you enjoy your first
"Closer Look"?

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.237
-Yeah, it was fine,
but I gotta get outta here.

00:08:58.237 --> 00:08:59.338
I have a doctor's appointment

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.274
I've been trying
to schedule forever.

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:03.976
[ Chuckle ] The webbing in one
of my feet is all messed up.

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:05.711 line:0%
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:09.348 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:10.650 line:0%
We've been talking
about City Harvest

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.818 line:0%
since COVID began
and, now, more than ever,

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:14.820 line:0%
they need your help
feeding New York families.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.189 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:19.591 line:0%
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:09:19.591 --> 00:09:22.028 line:0%
Wear a mask.
We love you.

